WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:07.100
There is a new poll of Ohio voters done by
the right leaning Rasmussen Reports, which

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.260
has Donald Trump losing by four points to
Joe Biden, 49 to 45.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:15.080
And this is a really important poll for a
few different reasons.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.180
First of all, is Ohio.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.230
Ohio is of such importance to Republicans
and in fact, Republicans.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:26.369
A Republican presidential candidate has not
won the Electoral College without winning

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:27.369
Ohio.

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:28.369
Dating back decades.

00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:30.949
You have to go at least to the 70s.

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:32.360
And I didn't go back any further than that.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:39.400
So Republicans need Ohio historically in order
to win, even more so than, I would even say,

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.400
Florida.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.170
Ohio is one of those states where if Trump
does not win Ohio, it could be a very, very

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:48.280
bad election for Donald Trump.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.080
This is also an important poll because it's
a Rasmussen poll and Rasmussen polls tend

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.750
to lean right.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.960
If even a Rasmussen poll says Trump is losing
Ohio by four.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.350
That could also be very bad for Trump.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.370
However, you might say this is only one poll.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:08.710
Donald Trump certainly is still winning Ohio
overall, right?

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.040
Not so fast.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:15.450
In fact, in the real Clear Politics average
of recent polling, Joe Biden is up by two

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.830
point four on average right now in Ohio.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:23.290
That includes an Ohio media collaborative
poll from six weeks ago which had Joe Biden

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.420
winning it.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:29.850
There's a poll between that one and the Rasmussen
poll, which has Donald Trump up by one.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:35.740
So it is certainly true that there's not as
much polling data out of Ohio as there is

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.979
from some other states.

00:01:36.979 --> 00:01:42.710
It is absolutely a fact that we should not
get cocky or arrogant in any way.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:48.940
But this is much like, you know, when we look
at Donald Trump being up by only two in Texas,

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:53.229
according to the recent Dallas Morning News
poll.

00:01:53.229 --> 00:02:00.049
When you look at the numbers out of places
like Arizona, these are signals about how

00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:04.080
the election could go if we vote, if that's
all it is.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:08.670
These are when I see a poll, I see it as an
opportunity.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:13.530
And it actually would make a lot of sense
if Ohio went to Joe Biden.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.940
It would make sense because Ohio has been
absolutely ravaged by Donald Trump's tariffs

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:21.370
on China, which I know you all understand
this.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:27.959
Trump doesn't seem to when you place tariffs
on Chinese products, American businesses importing

00:02:27.959 --> 00:02:30.260
those products pay the tariffs.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:35.450
It's not the Chinese who pay the tariffs when
you're in manufacturing, when you're in farming

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.960
and you're dealing with counter tariffs from
China.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:44.489
Ohio is a place that would be very much affected
by Donald Trump's disastrous trade policy.

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:48.069
The point here is every state has to be involved.

00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:49.810
We're going to deal with this in today's voicemail.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:56.650
In fact, I'm continuing to experience worry
that some people aren't getting the importance

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.390
of every state being involved here.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.110
But think about it this way.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:03.819
If Donald Trump is really up by only two in
Texas.

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:05.530
Make him fight for the win.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:11.390
Make him spend money in Texas that he won't
have other places.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:15.480
We talked yesterday about how Donald Trump
has already spent 73 percent of the one point

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.390
one billion dollars that he's raised since
the start of 2019.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:20.860
Trump is in a cash crunch.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:24.550
Trump is struggling to continue running ads
in all of the states in which he should be

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:28.200
running ads, make him spend money to defend
Texas.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:33.700
If Florida is tied or Bidens up a little in
Florida or Trump is up a little in Florida,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:39.420
the point is Florida is in play and any money
that Trump spends in Florida is money he cannot

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.430
spend in Ohio.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:42.590
That's good for Joe Biden.

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:48.230
The whole point here is we have to run up
the score in every state while simultaneously

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.519
keeping the pressure up.

00:03:49.519 --> 00:03:53.500
So Trump actually has to fight for states
that in past elections, Republicans didn't

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.879
have to put any money into.

00:03:54.879 --> 00:03:57.020
That would have been easy wins for Republicans.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.560
That's the way to do it.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.610
One other great example of this is Arizona.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:07.220
Arizona has been a red state for a long time
and in presidential elections.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:13.830
And on average, Joe Biden is currently winning
by five, including winning by nine in Arizona.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:18.820
In a recent Fox News poll, Martha McSally,
the Republican incumbent senator in Arizona,

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.550
is down by as much as 17.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:25.310
Two Democratic Senate challenger, Mark Kelly.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:32.750
It tells us nothing other than the state is
in play and it's worth fighting for, if only

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.550
to make Donald Trump himself have to fight
for it.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.910
That in itself helps Joe Biden.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.370
Let's keep it going.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:42.680
We're down to just seven plus weeks remaining
here.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.360
We're going to keep the pressure up.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:05:58.240
We need you to keep the pressure up as well.

